[h2]Better Sliders (Direct Numeric Input)[/h2]
Adds click-to-edit inline numeric input to sliders in both the game [b]Options[/b] window and [b]Mod Config[/b] windows. Instead of nudging a tiny slider thumb back and forth for exact values, just click the number next to any slider and type the value directly.

[list]
[*][b]Click Number to Edit Inline[/b]: Hovering a slider value highlights it subtly; clicking opens an inline input box right over the readout with the current value pre-selected so you can type immediately.
[*][b]Natural Keyboard & Focus Flow[/b]: Press [b]Enter[/b] (or Keypad Enter) or click outside to apply—automatically clamped to the slider's min/max bounds and rounded for integer sliders. Press [b]Esc[/b] to cancel editing and restore the previous value without closing the Options or Mod Config window.
[*][b]Seamless Apply & Reset[/b]: Clicking [b]Apply[/b] commits any active inline input first; clicking [b]Reset[/b] or dragging the slider cancels editing and syncs the display immediately.
[*][b]Completes Missing Float Readouts[/b]: Automatically adds a right-aligned, click-to-edit numeric readout to float sliders that lacked one (such as volume, dialogue speed, or mod sliders without a built-in value label).
[*][b]Supports Formatted & Percentage Sliders[/b]: Works with scaled or unit-suffixed displays (such as [b]100%[/b]), letting you type display values directly (e.g. [b]120[/b] or [b]120%[/b]).
[*][b]Respects Disabled Rules[/b]: Sliders disabled by game rules stay non-editable and dimmed in sync.
[/list]

[h3]Compatibility & Notes[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Save-safe & Zero Sensitive Capabilities[/b]: Pure UI quality-of-life enhancement; does not touch save files and declares empty Capabilities (no external reflection).
[/list]

